[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Cambridge Springs Defence, Bd3 trap"]
[ECO "D52"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pin"]
[Themes "queen-sortie,pin-on-c3"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "9.Bd3"]
[Start "cambridge-springs 7...Bb4"]

8. Qc2 ( 8. Qb3 dxc4 { The pawn takes with a threat on the queen, and the knight on c3 is pinned. } ) 8... O-O 9. Bd3 $2 { A natural developing move. It leaves the bishop on g5 without a defender. } 9... dxc4 $1 { Hits the bishop on d3 and opens the fifth rank, so the queen on a5 now attacks the bishop on g5. } 10. Nxc4 Qxg5 { White cannot save both bishops, and the pinned knight cannot help. } *
